      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Prototype a conservative Prim-side optimization, preserving the existing partition order and tie behavior. `Prim_ST` copies the graph and its matrices, and `find_min_key` copies vectors; use references and avoid redundant matrix copies where excluded edges can be checked without changing selection order. Verify the invariant that cycle checks are unnecessary: accepted edges join a newly selected vertex to an earlier vertex, while each tested candidate joins the current vertex to an unvisited one, so it cannot close a cycle in the selected forest. Preserve output formatting and compare outputs against the correctness oracle after each change.\",\"B\":\"Explore an alternative exact solver that searches simple paths in the original graph instead of enumerating spanning trees. Track visited vertices and per-color counts, update the best path as the search proceeds, and use only safe upper bounds (for example, current distinct colors plus all not-yet-seen colors in the component). Handle disconnected components independently; do not use incomplete memoization that ignores the visited-vertex state. This search may be exponential and can choose a different tied optimum than the reference, so retain it only if it passes the official correctness checks and required output behavior on the full suite.\",\"C\":\"Optimize the existing path-search hot path without changing its traversal order: build tree adjacency once per spanning tree in the same edge order, replace repeated scans of `arvoreGeradora`, and replace copied path histories and linear color-membership checks with in-place push/pop, visited markers, and incremental per-color counts. Preserve the current early-exit and first-best tie behavior, and verify exact oracle outputs as well as runtime.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only independently validated candidates, keeping a known-correct fallback. The sole measurement is a valid baseline: 4 cases, mean 0.0053626 s (samples 0.0054330, 0.0053846, 0.0052703), score 0.5; there are no candidate or interaction measurements. Treat this short runtime and small case count as noisy, limited evidence. Re-measure each integrated combination under the existing setup and judge by whole-run correctness and timing—do not assume gains add. The target is 4-core ARM64 with no GPU; account for threading overhead and avoid oversubscription. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source outside the assigned candidate work.\",\"analysis\":\"The source spends work on dense adjacency matrices, repeated graph/matrix/vector copies, cycle checks during Prim construction, repeated scans of spanning-tree edges, and copied path histories with linear color checks. These motivate a low-risk Prim pass (A), an independently measured exact-search alternative (B), and traversal-preserving path-search data-structure improvements (C). Because the official material describes reference-output comparison, changed tie behavior must not be presumed acceptable. G should select based on correctness and measured integrated performance, not theoretical or additive gains.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"410dbf16f33edb7838a6850d9dda270fa82b09e980e8d5453c264f5d9277a960\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Prototype a conservative Prim-side optimization, preserving the existing partition order and tie behavior. `Prim_ST` copies the graph and its matrices, and `find_min_key` copies vectors; use references and avoid redundant matrix copies where excluded edges can be checked without changing selection order. Verify the invariant that cycle checks are unnecessary: accepted edges join a newly selected vertex to an earlier vertex, while each tested candidate joins the current vertex to an unvisited one, so it cannot close a cycle in the selected forest. Preserve output formatting and compare outputs against the correctness oracle after each change.\",\"B\":\"Explore an alternative exact solver that searches simple paths in the original graph instead of enumerating spanning trees. Track visited vertices and per-color counts, update the best path as the search proceeds, and use only safe upper bounds (for example, current distinct colors plus all not-yet-seen colors in the component). Handle disconnected components independently; do not use incomplete memoization that ignores the visited-vertex state. This search may be exponential and can choose a different tied optimum than the reference, so retain it only if it passes the official correctness checks and required output behavior on the full suite.\",\"C\":\"Optimize the existing path-search hot path without changing its traversal order: build tree adjacency once per spanning tree in the same edge order, replace repeated scans of `arvoreGeradora`, and replace copied path histories and linear color-membership checks with in-place push/pop, visited markers, and incremental per-color counts. Preserve the current early-exit and first-best tie behavior, and verify exact oracle outputs as well as runtime.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only independently validated candidates, keeping a known-correct fallback. The sole measurement is a valid baseline: 4 cases, mean 0.0053626 s (samples 0.0054330, 0.0053846, 0.0052703), score 0.5; there are no candidate or interaction measurements. Treat this short runtime and small case count as noisy, limited evidence. Re-measure each integrated combination under the existing setup and judge by whole-run correctness and timing—do not assume gains add. The target is 4-core ARM64 with no GPU; account for threading overhead and avoid oversubscription. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source outside the assigned candidate work.\",\"analysis\":\"The source spends work on dense adjacency matrices, repeated graph/matrix/vector copies, cycle checks during Prim construction, repeated scans of spanning-tree edges, and copied path histories with linear color checks. These motivate a low-risk Prim pass (A), an independently measured exact-search alternative (B), and traversal-preserving path-search data-structure improvements (C). Because the official material describes reference-output comparison, changed tie behavior must not be presumed acceptable. G should select based on correctness and measured integrated performance, not theoretical or additive gains.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"c8fd1330443a43dd8328225562285d71\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"410dbf16f33edb7838a6850d9dda270fa82b09e980e8d5453c264f5d9277a960\",\"session_id\":\"c08531b8446a447bacb06c4500c0c033\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"8b136539f920e308162b0dd6a72b1150ad6d4f6b1528768b7100f6db9ca901e2\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":14595,\"output_tokens\":8526,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":7927}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":23121,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
