    {
      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research Prim_ST overhead: use cycle-check removal as a control and investigate avoiding per-call graph/matrix copies or scratch allocations, without changing include/exclude behavior or vertex-selection order. Preserve exact tie behavior and output; do not repeat the slower flat-matrix conversion without new evidence.\",\"B\":\"Focus on find_min_key: measure a simple sequential scan that avoids copying its inputs (for example, const references) while preserving signed-key ordering, first-index ties, and disconnected detection. The packed reduction was only marginally faster than baseline and the SIMD/byte-flag variant was slower; do not assume parallel reduction helps on this 4-core ARM64 target.\",\"C\":\"Investigate reducing dense graph setup and traversal work. The resize-plus-row-initialization candidate was fastest at 0.005211 s versus the 0.005363 s baseline; validate its benefit across general input sizes, and explore edge-oriented adjacency to avoid dense initialization/scans. Re-measure traversal parallelism and thresholds rather than tuning to the measured cases; preserve valid-input behavior and output ordering.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates with reviewed semantics and correctness evidence. Start by measuring the row-initialization and cycle-check-removal candidates individually, then test combinations: their gains are not additive by assumption. Use the existing correctness and measurement process unchanged, preserve output/tie behavior, and retain the fastest valid integration; do not modify tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source beyond integration.\",\"analysis\":\"The official problem is tropical paths in an undirected colored graph; the supplied source uses a dense adjacency matrix, repeated Prim-style spanning-tree work, and path traversal. On the 4-core ARM64 target, the baseline mean was 0.005363 s (correct on 4 cases). Individual reported means were 0.005211 s for parallel row initialization, 0.005236 s for removing the redundant cycle check, 0.005304 s for a packed reduction, and 0.005309 s for traversal changes. Contiguous-matrix/const-reference and SIMD/byte-flag candidates were slower at about 0.00551 s. These are small absolute differences from a short workload, so treat them as leads, not guarantees; correctness must remain primary.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"e9f1586244216d81eb801915a6ec2da9265e4d50ed18e74e53493d223f472435\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research Prim_ST overhead: use cycle-check removal as a control and investigate avoiding per-call graph/matrix copies or scratch allocations, without changing include/exclude behavior or vertex-selection order. Preserve exact tie behavior and output; do not repeat the slower flat-matrix conversion without new evidence.\",\"B\":\"Focus on find_min_key: measure a simple sequential scan that avoids copying its inputs (for example, const references) while preserving signed-key ordering, first-index ties, and disconnected detection. The packed reduction was only marginally faster than baseline and the SIMD/byte-flag variant was slower; do not assume parallel reduction helps on this 4-core ARM64 target.\",\"C\":\"Investigate reducing dense graph setup and traversal work. The resize-plus-row-initialization candidate was fastest at 0.005211 s versus the 0.005363 s baseline; validate its benefit across general input sizes, and explore edge-oriented adjacency to avoid dense initialization/scans. Re-measure traversal parallelism and thresholds rather than tuning to the measured cases; preserve valid-input behavior and output ordering.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidates with reviewed semantics and correctness evidence. Start by measuring the row-initialization and cycle-check-removal candidates individually, then test combinations: their gains are not additive by assumption. Use the existing correctness and measurement process unchanged, preserve output/tie behavior, and retain the fastest valid integration; do not modify tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source beyond integration.\",\"analysis\":\"The official problem is tropical paths in an undirected colored graph; the supplied source uses a dense adjacency matrix, repeated Prim-style spanning-tree work, and path traversal. On the 4-core ARM64 target, the baseline mean was 0.005363 s (correct on 4 cases). Individual reported means were 0.005211 s for parallel row initialization, 0.005236 s for removing the redundant cycle check, 0.005304 s for a packed reduction, and 0.005309 s for traversal changes. Contiguous-matrix/const-reference and SIMD/byte-flag candidates were slower at about 0.00551 s. These are small absolute differences from a short workload, so treat them as leads, not guarantees; correctness must remain primary.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"618feefe5ece4ecdab42f77921870574\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"e9f1586244216d81eb801915a6ec2da9265e4d50ed18e74e53493d223f472435\",\"session_id\":\"c08531b8446a447bacb06c4500c0c033\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"8ce8465588e0892212d7674313059316d7c7179da6731477251b42638fdac5ac\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":28985,\"output_tokens\":5936,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":5463}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":34921,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
